From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:51:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: ave: import the AVE encoder driver from aurora
 integration/aurora

Bring the Apple AVE (H.264/HEVC) V4L2 memory-to-memory encoder driver
over from the aurora integration/aurora branch (50d5865ea6, fetched
2026-11-08) as whole files, so that a T8132 variant can be added on top:

  drivers/media/platform/apple/ave/                         (whole dir)
  Documentation/admin-guide/media/apple-ave.rst
  Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,t8140-ave.yaml

and the one-line hooks integration/aurora has for it: the Kconfig source
and Makefile entry in drivers/media/platform/apple, the admin-guide media
index entry and CONFIG_VIDEO_APPLE_AVE=m in asahi.config. All imported
files are byte-identical to integration/aurora; this base has no AVE
code, so nothing local is overwritten. A per-commit cherry-pick is not
used because the history touches unrelated INT-only files.

The driver binds only to apple,t6000/t6041/t8112/t8140-ave, none of
which a J604 device tree has, so on its own this commit changes nothing
at runtime except building apple-ave.ko.

